# C# and .NET

- Target `net10.0` unless an existing project documents otherwise.
- Keep nullable reference types and implicit usings enabled.
- Prefer `TreatWarningsAsErrors` and modern analysis levels on production projects.
- Use constructor injection and options validation (`ValidateOnStart` / data annotations) for host apps.
- Prefer structured logging; do not log secrets or connection strings.
- Honor `CancellationToken` on async APIs; do not invent fire-and-forget work without ownership.
- Dispose/`await using` owned resources; document shared ownership explicitly.
- Treat concurrency and thread-safety as part of the contract, not an afterthought.
- Performance-sensitive paths need measured evidence before micro-optimization claims.
- Do not add NuGet packages without a concrete need; prefer framework packages already in use.
